<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Liliʻuokalani returns for her subsequent annual wellness visit, four weeks after her three-month stroke review, with two members of her ʻohana whom she asked to join her. She completed the health risk assessment beforehand. She has had no further nosebleeds since she began using a gel and a humidifier, no new neurological symptoms and no falls. She plays the piano every morning and has begun arranging a new song. She takes apixaban twice daily from a pill box and has missed no doses. She asked to talk about what she would want if she had a larger stroke. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, emergency visits or hospital stays since the stroke</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Atorvastatin, losartan and apixaban from a pill box; no over-the-counter medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Minor ischemic stroke, paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and hypertension, all managed</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities and instrumental activities of daily living</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with members of her household; close ʻohana and community; daily prayer; no loneliness</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; alcohol rarely; walks in her garden daily; less salted fish</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in bathing, dressing, eating, toileting and transfers</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages her medicines, correspondence and music; does not drive; others shop for the household</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; handrails on the stairs; bathroom floor slippery when wet</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hears well; reading glasses; eye examination last year</td></tr><tr><td>Bladder</td><td>No leakage</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns from her or her ʻohana</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

