    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed, personalized prevention plan updated and a written copy given. Depression, alcohol and cognitive screens are negative; fall risk is moderate because she takes an anticoagulant. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Minor ischemic stroke (I63.412)</content>. No recurrence; full recovery of the right hand and speech. [S]<list><item>Continue atorvastatin, losartan and apixaban.</item><item>Five-month review in six weeks with a lipid panel, kidney function and a blood count.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk on an anticoagulant</content>. No falls and a Timed Up and Go of 11 seconds, but a fall on apixaban could cause a serious bleed. [S]<list><item>Non-slip mat and a grab bar in the bathroom.</item><item>Balance and strength exercises from the falls-prevention program at the community center.</item><item>Call the clinic after any fall, and go to the emergency department after any blow to the head.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 today; no prior pneumococcal vaccine</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single dose today, for adults 75 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>This season&apos;s high-dose vaccine when it arrives in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Never given; first dose at the five-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Due</td><td>No record within ten years; Tdap at the five-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Osteopenia on a scan three years ago; repeat now because a fracture on an anticoagulant carries extra risk</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 18 to 79; never tested; blood drawn today, result by telephone</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Evidence is insufficient after 75; after discussion she chose to stop mammograms</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Normal colonoscopy at 70; at 76 to 85 screening is selective, and after discussion she chose not to continue</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 65 with adequate prior screening</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker; aneurysm screening applies to men who have smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5; MoCA 26 at the stroke clinic</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; bathroom safety and an exercise program</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure, cholesterol and diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Blood pressure at every visit; LDL 64 mg/dL at the five-week review; hemoglobin A1c 5.5% at intake</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Respiratory syncytial virus vaccine, single dose [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: DXA booked; hepatitis C result by telephone. Five-month review in six weeks. Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines in the autumn. Next annual wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-24: five-month review: blood pressure, lipids, apixaban safety, cognition and plans for the months ahead. [S]</paragraph></text>

