    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 25 minutes, with her consent and with the two members of her ʻohana she invited. She named one of them, whom she raised as hānai, as her health care agent on the Hawaiʻi advance health care directive, now copied into the chart. She wants full treatment for a stroke or illness she could recover from, including clot-removal treatment if it were offered in time. If a severe stroke left her unable to speak, understand or know her ʻohana, with little hope of recovery, she would not want resuscitation, a breathing machine or tube feeding, and would want to be cared for at home in comfort, with her ʻohana and her minister with her and with her own Hawaiian practices as she and her ʻohana choose. She asked that her agent make decisions together with the ʻohana, while respecting what she has said today. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
